module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.unapplied_function_value_admitted_at_a_value_position

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data unapplied_function_value_admitted_at_a_value_position: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "unapplied_function_value_admitted_at_a_value_position" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a nullary function's NAME, written where a VALUE of that function's return type is declared, is accepted with no diagnostic. empty_map stands where empty_map() was meant, so the position holds a fn() -> Map<String, Bool> where a Map<String, Bool> is required. ",

    "HARM: the author reads a clean compile as verification of the seam the change introduced. That is the specification-without-execution shape of DESIGN section 5 arriving through the compiler rather than around it, which is worse than the ordinary form because the clean compile is the very artifact the author is entitled to trust. ",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACT, AND IT IS WHAT MAKES THIS A GAP RATHER THAN A LIMIT: the refusal is REACHABLE AT THE SAME POSITION IN THE SAME COMPILE. A String at a CONCRETE parameter declared Map<String, Bool> is refused, located and typed; an unapplied nullary function at that IDENTICAL position is accepted. So the checker decides shape at this position and does not decide THIS shape. ",

    "THE INSTRUMENT, NAMED RATHER THAN TRANSCRIBED (DESIGN section 6): test.claim.argument_shape_at_a_declared_position_probe_test, which hands the compiler four sources through gunbc.compile_diagnostic_census compile_dag_diagnostic_census and folds each to a blocking-diagnostic count. Re-derive with claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/test/claim/argument_shape_at_a_declared_position_probe_test.dag and the four function names it declares. The counts are not copied here, because a copied count is unreachable from the producer that owns it and rots without anyone touching either end. ",

    "WHY THE FIXTURE IS SOURCE HANDED TO THE COMPILER RATHER THAN A CORPUS MODULE, since that is the question a reader will ask first: two of the four programs are INVALID and one is correctly refused, so as corpus members they would break every build that resolved them. DESIGN section 4b rules exactly this case -- a state unrepresentable in the accepted corpus may still be representable as source handed to the compiler by a fixture, and a compiler is a thing whose regression probes are invalid programs. The refusal is authorable there, so the evidence is enrollable there. ",

    "AND THE MISMATCH IS DECIDABLE WITHOUT DECIDING ANYTHING ELSE. No instantiation of any type variable makes fn() -> T inhabit T, because a function type and its result type are different constructors. The judgment needs the argument's own shape and nothing about the declared position beyond its being a non-function type. ",

    "THIS IS NOT THE GENERIC-FORMAL DEFERRAL AND MUST NOT BE FOLDED INTO IT. The position an_unapplied_function_at_a_concrete_position_is_refused exercises is CONCRETE. The generic-formal population is owned by generic_application_admits_distinct_unit_variant_arguments, whose ceiling sentence this same fixture discharges in a separate receipt there; that row's subject is variant identity at a generic position, and this row's subject is a function value at a concrete one. Two mechanisms, one consequence -- a decidable mismatch admitted -- and folding them would let a repair for either be credited to both. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: outside the ladder. The invalid state is accepted with no diagnostic at all, so nothing is mitigated, and an accepted wrong program is not a rung. CEILING: structurally impossible, and the ceiling is DERIVED rather than aspirational -- the class is decidable from the argument alone, its authority is the same declared-type judgment that already refuses a_string_at_a_concrete_position_is_refused's source, and 'undecidable' is not available as an excuse here because the sibling diagnostic's own name has been measured not to be a limit. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the declared-type judgment decides FUNCTION-TYPE-AGAINST-NON-FUNCTION-TYPE from the argument's own shape before it consults the declared position, sufficient that an_unapplied_function_at_a_concrete_position_is_refused reaches a located, typed refusal in the same compile in which a_string_at_a_concrete_position_is_refused already does. Nothing else retires this row. The trigger names that capability rather than the fixture, because a fixture that merely exists would satisfy a fixture-shaped trigger while the capability stayed dead. ",

    "EVIDENCE OBLIGATION ON THE CLIMB, AND THE HONEST STANDING IS THAT IT IS NOT YET DISCHARGED. The probe module lands with this row and carries three shape arms and a well-typed control: the unapplied-function arm asserts REFUSAL and is the discriminating RED; the String-at-a-concrete-position arm asserts refusal, is green today, and is the positive control that makes the first arm mean something rather than being indistinguishable from a broken fixture; the String-at-a-generic-position arm is the one whose result discharges the CEILING SENTENCE of generic_application_admits_distinct_unit_variant_arguments -- NOT that row's subject, which is variant identity rather than shape; and a well-typed call asserts zero blocking diagnostics so an import typo cannot red the others and read as walls landing. ",

    "THE REQUIRED FLOOR DOES RUN THESE FOUR IDENTITIES, AND AN EARLIER REVISION OF THIS ROW SAID IT DID NOT. The module matches NO prefix in v2.workflow.required_floor required_gate_prefixes, and that is true and is not the whole admission rule: the floor ALSO plans a witness whose file the change touches. The landing run's own required-floor-disposition artifact carries all four of these identities at disposition planned_as_changed_witness, with the two expecting-red arms recorded known-red-held. RE-DERIVE IT RATHER THAN READING A NUMBER HERE: download the required-floor-disposition artifact from any completed witnesses run on a change that touches this module -- gh run download <run id> -R gunb-ai/gunbc -n required-floor-disposition -- and read the rows for this module's identities BY HEADER NAME, disposition and outcome. No count is copied into this row, including the census denominator: the load-bearing claim is the disposition these four identities carry, which needs no denominator, and a transcribed census size is a run-local number nothing re-derives. So the module is dormant on ORDINARY floors and RUN on every change that touches it, which necessarily includes the change that lands it. Reading the prefix roster alone and concluding 'discovered, not run' was reasoning about a subject the artifact answers directly. ",

    "AND THAT IS WHY THE TWO REDS ARE ENROLLED IN v2.workflow.floor_expected_red RATHER THAN LEFT OFF IT. An earlier revision REMOVED that enrolment on the belief that it asserted something false. The roster's rule is that enrolling an identity asserts it REACHES ITS SUBJECT AND ANSWERS, and the disposition artifact shows exactly that: both arms evaluate and return false with cause claim_failed, which is a reached answer and not a never-executed row. The 101 rows the roster's header records as removed were removed for the opposite condition -- identities that never ran at all, reading as debt someone was working. Un-enrolled, these two block their own landing change while documenting a defect the row admits is real. ",

    "THE EXECUTING CONSUMER OUTSIDE A CHANGE TO THIS MODULE IS STILL THE NAMED claim_batch INVOCATION, and the gap this row reports is unchanged by the correction above: no ORDINARY floor run repeats this measurement, so between changes the rung rests on a human-run command. Admitting the module to required_gate_prefixes is what would make a required lane run these rows on every change rather than only on changes that touch them. ",

    "SO THE RUNG THIS ROW REPORTS RESTS ON A HUMAN-RUN COMMAND RATHER THAN A GATE, and that is the gap, not a decoration. Admitting the module to required_gate_prefixes is what would convert the probe from re-derivable evidence into ENROLLED evidence, and only then is an expected-red enrolment both true and necessary. Until then this row's rung is established by an executed measurement that no required consumer repeats. ",

    "THE ASSERTIONS ARE THE CORRECT BEHAVIOUR, NOT THE OBSERVED ONE, and that is deliberate. Written the other way -- asserting that the function arm is accepted -- the row would go green today and become a DEFENDER OF THE DEFECT, cited afterwards as coverage of a wall that does not exist. It flips green of its own accord when the wall lands, and per DESIGN section 4b meta-obligation (4) it does not retire then: it converts to a permanent regression control. ",

    "THE STALL IS TRACKED RATHER THAN PARKED, and that is what keeps an unrouted red from becoming an untracked stall. gunbc.guarantee_stall.argument_shape_undecided_at_a_declared_position_stall carries the subject, the rung, the derived ceiling and TWO triggers at different grains -- the compiler capability that retires the class, and separately the required_gate_prefixes admission that would make a required lane run these rows at all. NO ROSTER EXIT IS CLAIMED HERE, AND THAT IS NOT BECAUSE THE IDENTITIES ARE OFF THE ROSTER -- they are enrolled in v2.workflow.floor_expected_red, for the reason stated above. It is because DESIGN section 4b(4) is explicit that a climb dissolves production handling and never the evidence: on the day both rows reach a located, typed refusal they flip to permanent regression controls and STAY enrolled. An earlier revision of this sentence read the enrolment the other way and said they were not on the roster at all, which contradicted this row's own receipt two fields above. What the stall's trigger actually says is that on the day both rows reach a located, typed refusal they flip to permanent regression controls per DESIGN section 4b(4). ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: when a compile over a change comes back clean, ask whether any argument the change introduced is a bare function name at a position declared as a value. The behavioural tell is that the defect is found by a READER rather than by the compiler, on a diff the compiler reported nothing about.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
